4554:./orchestration/tickets/W2-removals/impl-review.out:27:A. DANGLING REFERENCES / ORPHANED IMPORTS. Any remaining reference (import, call, type, event kind, error code, SQL column) to removed machinery: the plan-tree/replan subsystem (days/logic/tree.py, days/logic/effects.py, PlanTree/PlanNode/PlanRoot/NodeStatus, load_plan/store_plan/apply_plan_effects, submit_replan/process_pending_replan/reset_replan_queue, replan_root/replan_child, plan_* EventKinds); boundary_runs table + _boundary_ran/_record_boundary; seed route/CLI/demo (seed/api.py, seed/demo.py, the `seed` CLI verb, ErrorCode.db_not_empty); sprint freeze/addenda (freeze.py, freeze_kickoff/freeze_review, add_addendum, Addendum/AddendumBody, weekly_addenda/kickoff_frozen_at/review_frozen_at columns, kickoff_frozen/review_frozen/addendum_added EventKinds); sprint_items.current_state_note; days.plan column; the title_max_chars config knob (Config field, load_config line, PLAN_TITLE_MAX_CHARS env, config.yaml key, the startup assert). Note: the parameter NAME title_max_chars on create_ticket/validate_title is intentionally kept — not a defect.
4556:./orchestration/tickets/W2-removals/impl-review.out:33:D. W3 EXCLUSION-LIST BREACHES (highest priority). Confirm NONE of these were altered: the `runs` table; tickets.claim_lock/claim_expires/alias/auto_blocked/consecutive_failures columns; X-Plan-Run-Id/X-Plan-Claim headers; the `run` CLI group; all of src/planner/dispatch/*; the breaker; budget/concurrency/timeout config keys (max_runs, failure_limit, run_max_seconds, claim_ttl_seconds, tick_seconds, dispatch_enabled, dispatcher_lock_path); the dispatcher lock. The seed importer must still INSERT auto_blocked/consecutive_failures; tickets/data.py must still own claim columns.
4557:./orchestration/tickets/W2-removals/impl-review.out:35:E. BOUNDARY GUARD REWORK CORRECTNESS. days/boundary.py replaced the boundary_runs dedup guard with `_next_day_materialized(conn, ndid)` checked at the TOP of run_boundary (before the deterministic pass), and run_boundary now returns str|None (None=guarded skip, "skipped"=human-planned, "failed", "ok"). days/scheduler.py::run_boundary_tick returns {planning_date, ran (=outcome is not None), judgment (=outcome)} — the "replan" key is gone. Verify: (1) once-per-date idempotence still holds; (2) the return-value contract is internally consistent with its callers (core/loops.py discards it; core/testmode.py returns it verbatim; the e2e/unit assertions); (3) flag the KNOWN edge that a human day-ticket (which materializes the day) now trips the top guard BEFORE _human_planned — so run_boundary returns None and the deterministic pass is skipped for that date. The implementer asserts this is the accepted edge per plan §14.4 and adapted test_a18 Part 3 to assert the guarded-skip (None) behavior instead of §11's "keeps its structure". Confirm this is coherent, or object with specifics.
