5017:./orchestration/tickets/W2-removals/impl-review.out:2563:./orchestration/tickets/W2-removals/impl-review.out:27:A. DANGLING REFERENCES / ORPHANED IMPORTS. Any remaining reference (import, call, type, event kind, error code, SQL column) to removed machinery: the plan-tree/replan subsystem (days/logic/tree.py, days/logic/effects.py, PlanTree/PlanNode/PlanRoot/NodeStatus, load_plan/store_plan/apply_plan_effects, submit_replan/process_pending_replan/reset_replan_queue, replan_root/replan_child, plan_* EventKinds); boundary_runs table + _boundary_ran/_record_boundary; seed route/CLI/demo (seed/api.py, seed/demo.py, the `seed` CLI verb, ErrorCode.db_not_empty); sprint freeze/addenda (freeze.py, freeze_kickoff/freeze_review, add_addendum, Addendum/AddendumBody, weekly_addenda/kickoff_frozen_at/review_frozen_at columns, kickoff_frozen/review_frozen/addendum_added EventKinds); sprint_items.current_state_note; days.plan column; the title_max_chars config knob (Config field, load_config line, PLAN_TITLE_MAX_CHARS env, config.yaml key, the startup assert). Note: the parameter NAME title_max_chars on create_ticket/validate_title is intentionally kept — not a defect.
5019:./orchestration/tickets/W2-removals/impl-review.out:2565:./orchestration/tickets/W2-removals/impl-review.out:35:E. BOUNDARY GUARD REWORK CORRECTNESS. days/boundary.py replaced the boundary_runs dedup guard with `_next_day_materialized(conn, ndid)` checked at the TOP of run_boundary (before the deterministic pass), and run_boundary now returns str|None (None=guarded skip, "skipped"=human-planned, "failed", "ok"). days/scheduler.py::run_boundary_tick returns {planning_date, ran (=outcome is not None), judgment (=outcome)} — the "replan" key is gone. Verify: (1) once-per-date idempotence still holds; (2) the return-value contract is internally consistent with its callers (core/loops.py discards it; core/testmode.py returns it verbatim; the e2e/unit assertions); (3) flag the KNOWN edge that a human day-ticket (which materializes the day) now trips the top guard BEFORE _human_planned — so run_boundary returns None and the deterministic pass is skipped for that date. The implementer asserts this is the accepted edge per plan §14.4 and adapted test_a18 Part 3 to assert the guarded-skip (None) behavior instead of §11's "keeps its structure". Confirm this is coherent, or object with specifics.
5039:./orchestration/tickets/W2-removals/impl-review.out:2720:./orchestration/tickets/T01-contracts/ticket.md:13:3. `src/planner/core/` — `config.py` (dataclass, YAML + `PLAN_*` env overrides, test-mode flags; fail-safe read semantics for dispatch_enabled), `clock.py` (Clock protocol; real; test clock honoring `PLAN_FAKE_NOW` only when `PLAN_TEST_MODE=1`, mutable for the set-now test endpoint), `ids.py` (prefixed slugs `sp_ si_ t_ idea_`, `day_YYYY-MM-DD`), `db.py` (WAL connect + full DDL: sprints, sprint_items, tickets, days, day_tickets, ideas, links, events, runs, boundary_runs — fields exactly per SPEC §3/§7.3/§6.2; `chat_session_key` on both tickets and days; tickets carry `alias`, `claim_lock`, `claim_expires`, `consecutive_failures`; events append-only AUTOINCREMENT), `events.py` (append_event; no update/delete path), `errors.py` (PlannerError with `code`, `message`, `detail`; JSON shape `{"error": {code, message, detail}}`; error-code constants), `contracts.py` (EventKind constants incl. spec-named `state_changed`, `proposal_accepted`, `proposal_superseded`, `day_ticket_removed`, `day_closed`, `auto_blocked`; LinkKind enum), `adapters/` (Protocols: SpawnAdapter, BoundaryAdapter with judgment + replan-root + replan-child, GatewayAdapter; fakes: scripted spawn, scripted boundary/replan, echo gateway + offline gateway; real implementations as thin stubs wired to config; registry selecting real/fake from config+test mode), `server.py` (FastAPI app factory shell mounting domain routers, static `assets/`, WS stub, test-mode router stub).
