11938:1. [system_b.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/system_b.py:105): continuing runs capture `chat_session_key` before they actually execute. If run A resumes `stored-key-1` and persists a rotated `stored-key-2`, a run B already submitted at lines 113-116 still resumes the stale key. A later run can also queue under `stored-key-2` while B is active under `stored-key-1`, splitting one ticket mind across two `MindQueue` keys and violating the per-session serialization contract.  
11939:Fix: serialize same-ticket dispatch through key resolution plus run completion, or re-resolve immediately before `_run` and requeue when the DB key differs. Add a test with two continuing `set_off`s where the first resume rotates the key and assert the second resumes the rotated key.
11941:2. [system_b.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/system_b.py:170): after the start write sets `agent_working`, unexpected exceptions from `run_step` or the invariant path skip the end write and leave the ticket stuck `agent_working`. `run_step` catches expected `GatewayError`s, but the injected `spawn` seam can raise non-`OSError` exceptions, and system code can still fail after line 161.  
11946:F1-F6 from plan review are otherwise addressed: auto-accept is covered through the real proposal writer, queue key is `session_key`, the machine lock is preserved, `_Unset` is typed, fake gateways are fresh per spawn, and the importer no longer inserts removed columns.
